 Returns `this` (the instance).
 
-#### .onEmpty()
+#### .onEmpty(options?)
 
 Returns a promise that settles when the queue becomes empty.
 
 Can be called multiple times. Useful if you for example add additional items at a later time.
 
-#### .onIdle()
+Both `.onEmpty()` and `.onIdle()` accept an optional `{signal: AbortSignal}` object, for example `await queue.onIdle({signal: controller.signal})`. Aborting rejects only that wait with `signal.reason` and does not affect queued or running tasks or other waits. An already-aborted signal rejects even if the queue is already empty or idle. The wait's event and abort listeners are removed when it settles. Calling either method without options keeps the existing behavior.
+
+#### .onIdle(options?)
 
 Returns a promise that settles when the queue becomes empty, and all promises have completed; `queue.size === 0 && queue.pending === 0`.
 
